    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Roz MacLean is a 41-year-old "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "dollhouse",
            "ref": "v-dollhouse"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " lover. Four years ago, she began to teach herself to make tiny designs by watching videos on the internet. Since then, she has been making lovely mini food to fill her dollhouse."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Each of the dishes Roz makes is no bigger than a large coin. How does she do that? Well, first, she "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "moulds",
            "ref": "v-mould"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "clay",
            "zh": "黏土"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into different shapes. Then, she uses "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "chalk pastels",
            "zh": "彩色粉笔"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", a small knife and even a toothbrush to get the details. Finally, she puts the dishes in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "oven",
            "ref": "v-oven"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and heats them for 30 minutes. Here comes the “delicious” food! Then, she will put the dishes in her beautiful dollhouse."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Roz’s designs include everything from lemon cakes to salt pork. After she posted photos of them on the internet, many people from different parts of the world wanted to buy her works. The prices for these “little meals” "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "range",
            "ref": "v-range"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from $7 to $35."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now Roz even has a tiny food workshop in her home. Her two young boys, aged nine and four, sometimes help her with the designs. “I’ve always loved tiny things and enjoyed building up my shop,” said Roz. “It has "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "brought in",
            "ref": "v-bring-in"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " some income—and, more importantly, so much joy!”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
